{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>ויקהל</b> It is written above 'כי קרן עור פניו' (that the skin of his face shone), and adjacent to it is the portion of Shabbat, to teach that the radiance of the face on Shabbat is not like that of the other days. And he said 'ויקהל' (and he assembled) because he came to state the portion of Shabbat — a hint that on Shabbatot and festivals they assemble to hear the derashah:" "<b> לעשות</b> The letters ל' and ת' equal 9 and it is defective of vav, to teach: 39 melakhot are done in 6 days and not on Shabbat. And likewise 'אשר ברא אלהים לעשות' (which Elohim created to do) — in 'ויכולו' you find acts of making and creations and melakhot and existences and emergences and separations, all of them 39 corresponding to 6. 39 melakhot, excluding their toladot. And likewise you find from 'ויקהל' until 'לא תבערו וגו' ביום השבת' — 39 words, excluding the word 'השבת': He mentioned 'לא תבערו' because the kindling of fire is needed for the melakhah of the Mishkan: to cook spices and to dye and to refine the silver and copper and gold:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:08.586086492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}